    "unit": 35,
    "title": "Expressing Regret and Criticism",
    "title_ko": "후회와 비판 표현",
    "focus_axis": "grammar"
  },
  "context": {
    "explanation_en": "Combining 'should have' with softening language keeps criticism constructive: 'I understand why you did it, but you probably should have asked first.' Pairing criticism with empathy ('I understand ..., but ...') is more diplomatic than a blunt 'should have' alone.",
    "explanation_ko": "'should have'를 완화 표현과 결합하면 비판이 건설적으로 들립니다: 'I understand why you did it, but you probably should have asked first.' 비판을 공감('I understand ..., but ...')과 함께 쓰면 단순한 'should have'보다 더 외교적입니다.",
    "key_expressions": [
      {
        "en": "I understand your reasoning, but you should have consulted the team.",
        "ko": "이유는 이해하지만 팀과 상의했어야 했어요."
      },
      {
        "en": "In hindsight, we probably shouldn't have rushed the decision.",
        "ko": "돌이켜보면 우리는 아마 결정을 서두르지 말았어야 했어요."
      },
      {
        "en": "It's easy to say now, but you could have handled that better.",
        "ko": "지금 말하기는 쉽지만, 그 상황을 더 잘 다룰 수 있었을 거예요."
      }
    ]
  },
  "tasks": [
    {
